From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bpereira <bpereira@cloudflare.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 23:42:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Keep the id map keyed by atom and out of shadow trees

The document's id map maps an id to the node that carries it. Key it by the interned atom rather
than a copied string, so an entry costs the atom's storage rather than its own allocation.

A shadow tree's ids are not document ids, so a move must not leave one in the map: the map is
rebuilt for the document tree, and a shadow node's entry would answer for an id the document no
longer has.
